From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: audio renderer clock check, rate support and stream service, kept activation object, session Stop/Pause without topology, topology loader error order

Behaviour recorded by todo_wine marks of mf's conformance tests:

- The audio renderer's SetPresentationClock fails with
  MF_E_CLOCK_NO_TIME_SOURCE for a clock without a time source (the clock is
  not kept).
- The audio renderer exposes IMFRateSupport (on the sink and through
  MF_RATE_CONTROL_SERVICE, also from the stream sink) and the stream sink
  exposes IMFGetService. Slowest rate is 0, fastest is +-2 (assumption, the
  tests only check success), thinning is not distinguished; E_POINTER first,
  then MF_E_SHUTDOWN, then MF_E_NOT_INITIALIZED without a current type;
  IsRateSupported reports the nearest supported rate.
- ShutdownObject of the audio renderer / video renderer activation objects
  keeps the shut down object: ActivateObject returns the same instance (which
  reports MF_E_SHUTDOWN). The sample grabber keeps its own MF_E_SHUTDOWN.
- A media session without a topology answers Stop and Pause with
  MESessionStopped / MESessionPaused carrying MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST.
- The topology loader reports MF_E_TOPO_UNSUPPORTED for a topology without
  connected branches before complaining about an unresolved sink activate
  (MF_E_TOPO_SINK_ACTIVATES_UNSUPPORTED), and drops its "stub" FIXME.

The todo_wine marks that now pass are removed.
